==================================================
PROJECT PURPOSE
==================================================

GUI is a detailed, animated robotic companion and device-control
assistant for an Android phone mounted inside a custom 3D-printed
MOBI Exo Suit.

The phone display becomes GUI's face.

GUI should:

- look alive
- respond to touch
- respond to gestures
- react to sound
- optionally react to visual motion
- listen for wake words
- understand voice commands
- speak naturally
- allow interruption while speaking
- open installed applications
- perform web searches
- control supported media playback
- open casting controls
- trigger registered Android automations
- optionally use Shizuku for advanced device actions
- provide an authenticated owner shell console
- communicate status through facial expressions and spoken responses

This must be a native Android application built with:

- Kotlin
- Jetpack Compose
- Compose Canvas
- coroutines
- StateFlow
- DataStore
- lifecycle-aware Android components

Do not create a web wrapper.

Create a complete, compilable Android project.

Do not leave placeholder TODO implementations for the core face,
settings, speech, command, app-launching, or web-search functionality.

