12. BARGE-IN AND INTERRUPTION
==================================================

Interruption is mandatory.

The user must not have to wait for GUI to finish speaking before giving
another command.

All three wake words must support interruption:

- GUI
- DUDE
- BROHAM

If GUI is speaking and detects any enabled wake word:

1. Stop TTS playback immediately.
2. Cancel streaming synthesis.
3. Flush queued speech.
4. Cancel the previous response job where appropriate.
5. Cancel nonessential work associated only with the old response.
6. Change the face from SPEAKING to ATTENTIVE.
7. Begin listening to the new command immediately.
8. Never resume the abandoned spoken response.

Also interrupt GUI when:

- the user taps the face while GUI is speaking
- the user performs the push-to-talk gesture
- the user presses Listen
- the user performs a two-finger emergency-stop tap
- user speech is detected during an enabled follow-up conversation
  window

Example:

GUI:
"Here are the results I found for..."

User:
"Dude, open Spotify."

GUI must stop the old sentence immediately and process the Spotify
command.

Example:

GUI:
"Working on..."

User:
"Broham, stop."

GUI must stop the appropriate interruptible operation.

BARGE-IN REQUIREMENTS:

- immediate TTS cancellation
- no delayed continuation
- no speaking over the user
- close the old recognition or response job
- start the new listening session
- update the face instantly
- prevent stale completion callbacks from restarting old speech

Prevent GUI from interpreting its own speaker output as user speech.

Use available Android audio-focus and echo-management strategies.

Use a short configurable playback suppression period when needed.

SETTINGS:

- Allow Interruption ON/OFF
- Interrupt by Wake Word ON/OFF
- Interrupt by Tap ON/OFF
- Conversation Follow-Up Window:
  - Off
  - 5 seconds
  - 10 seconds
  - 20 seconds

Two-finger tap must always stop speech, regardless of standard
interruption settings.

