38. MOST IMPORTANT DESIGN RULE
==================================================

GUI IS A CHARACTER, NOT A CHAT WINDOW.

When GUI listens, the face listens.

When GUI thinks, the eyes, brows, cheek lights, circuits, and jaw react.

When GUI works, the face stays alive.

When GUI speaks, the mouth aperture and jaw illumination move subtly.

When the user interrupts, GUI stops talking immediately and listens.

When GUI succeeds, the face communicates success.

When GUI is confused, the face communicates confusion.

When the user says "GUI," GUI responds normally.

When the user says "Dude," GUI responds with a subtle casual reaction.

When the user says "Broham," GUI gives a subtle confident reaction and
brief heroic jaw illumination.

The finished application should feel like a detailed, heroic robotic
buddy named GUI living inside the physical MOBI Exo Suit.